  "problem": {
    "statement": "### Is there an existing issue for the same feature request?\n\n- [x] I have checked the existing issues.\n\n### Is your feature request related to a problem?\n\n```Markdown\nIt's not a problem. But a large part of our local KB is epub files. We can unpack the epub files to folders of htmls. However, it would be better to have a native support of epub files directly.\n```\n\n\n### Describe the feature you'd like\n\nNative support of Epub filetype.\r\n\r\n\n\n### Describe implementation you've considered\n\nThe epub files are simply a bunch of packed htmls with clear structures. It would be easy to bridge the gap between epub and current processes of RAGFlow.\n\n### Documentation, adoption, use case\n\n```Markdown\nRAGFlow would have direct access to current storage of epubs, which is a high quality of information\n```\n\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_",
